# ===============================================
# Azure OpenAI configuration
# Azure OpenAI endpoint and API version / Mandatory when using Azure OpenAI
# Below variables added for Azure OpenAI configuration. The endpoint and API version are mandatory when using Azure OpenAI, regardless of the authentication method (API key or Azure CLI). If you are directly using OpenAI's API and not using Azure OpenAI at all, you can leave these variables empty as they will be ignored in that case.
# ===============================================
AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://your-endpoint.openai.azure.com/
AZURE_OPENAI_API_VERSION=2025-04-01-preview

# If you are not using AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY and not using OPENAI_API_KEY or NOT using any other direct API key
# And you must use az login and direct az credentials and bearer token for authentication, you still need to specify the endpoint and API version for the Azure OpenAI client configuration as above, but you can leave the AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY empty and the code will handle authentication via Azure CLI.
# you need to specify the CA certificate bundle path if you are in an environment that requires it for SSL verification. 
# CA Bundle configuration for SSL verification in corporate environments with TLS inspection. This can be set to a custom path if needed, or the code will attempt to build a combined bundle from certifi and any exported PEMs in %TEMP%\bosch-ca.
# Follow "https://inside-docupedia.bosch.com/confluence/spaces/AzureIMG/pages/1179022413/Azure+CLI"
# Below variables added to handle the case when users want to use az login for authentication with Azure OpenAI instead of using API keys. In such cases, users still need to specify the AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT and AZURE_OPENAI_API_VERSION for the client configuration, but they can leave the AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY empty. The code will detect that the API key is not set and will attempt to authenticate using Azure CLI credentials, which is useful in environments where managing API keys is not ideal and users can leverage their existing Azure credentials. Additionally, we need to specify the REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE for SSL verification in corporate environments with TLS inspection, ensuring that the client can properly verify SSL certificates when making requests to Azure OpenAI.
REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE=C:\Users\BHS1RNG\Downloads\azure_cli_cert.pem

